  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline study Lake Turkana, Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This study will give local governments of Marsabit and Turkana the tools and insight needed to manage the lake sustainably and create a pathway for sustainable development of the fisheries sector an contributing to employment and improved food security. Updated knowledge regarding the lake&apos;s Maximum Sustainable Yield and stock level status will allow local governments to determine how much fish can be caught annually sustainably. Understanding the water level&apos;s effect will enable local authorities to use this information for years. It will also assist development partners in developing sustainable intervention in support of the County Governments.</narrative>
  </description>
